  "description_text": "Welcome to your Logan Square home. This 1908 Chicago workers cottage sits on one of the neighborhood's most coveted tree-lined streets, steps from restaurants, shops, nightlife, the farmers market, and the CTA. Thoughtfully restored, it keeps its original character while living like a modern home. A welcoming front porch opens to a large living room that flows into a separate dining room with a built-in hutch. A flexible den is made for movie nights, and a main-floor bedroom or office gives you room to spread out. The remodeled kitchen delivers custom cabinetry, new appliances, and a huge walk-in pantry. It opens to a bright back sunroom overlooking the lush, fully fenced backyard and detached garage. Upstairs, two generous bedrooms include a primary with a walk-in closet plus a second closet. The fully remodeled bath features a walk-in shower and abundant natural light. The updates match the charm: three mini-split A/C units, newer Pella windows, and countless improvements throughout. The home earned the Driehaus Bungalow Green Designation, proof you can be over a century old and still the smartest house on the block. The full unfinished basement has great ceiling height and endless potential: rec room, home gym, workshop, or studio. They call it a \"workers cottage,\" but the hard work is already done. Welcome home!",
